1. `To access second digit of any number N` : from right hand side  `(n/10)%10` and if third then again
    divide ((n/10))/10 and then take modulo and if want first digit then direct take modulo . 
    
    
2. `To remove 2nd last of a number N` : `(N%10) + (N/100)*10`


3. `Bitwise operators working` : sometimes for some bitwise operators despite they are of same in decimal
    system but represented in differnt number of bits in binary system then they may give different or 
    unexpected answers. 
    
    
4. `10 bitwise operators trick for cp` : bitwise operators are really fast .
		1. `Number is odd or even` : `n & 1 ` if this is true then the number is odd otherwise even . this will
	        check least significant bit with 1 and if that is 1 then number will 1 otherwise 0 .  And this is much 
	        much faster than `x % 2` . 
		2. `To check wether any number's prime factors are only and only 2` :then use `x & (x-1)` return 0 (means 
		    false) then yes otherwise no. (but make sure this give bug on 0 and 1).
		3. `playing with kth bit` : First kth bit refering to kth bit from right hand side . 
			1. `check if kth bit is set` : A bit is "set" when its value at that specific binary position is `1` `x & (1 << k)` 
			2. `toggle the kth bit` : `x ^ (1<<k)` means reversing the bit if 1 then 0 if 0 then 1. 
			3. `set the kth bit` : `x | (1<<k)` we can set the kth bit.
			4. `unset the kth bit` : `x & ~(1 << k)` . 
		4. `multiply or divide any number by 2 raise to k` : `a >> k` then this a will get divided by 2 raise to k . `a*(1 << k)`
		    then a will get multipled by 2 raise to k .
		5. `finding out x modulo 2 raise to k` : `x & ((1<<k)-1)`.
		6. `Swapping numbers without creating a temporary variable` : `a = a^b;b = a^b;a = a^b;` after writing these 3 
		    lines a and b will get swapped. 
		7. `a important propery of bitwise operators` : number of set bits in A = X , number of set bits in B = y number of
		    set bitgs in (A ^ B) = Z . then Z is even if X+Y is even , Z is odd if X+Y is odd . 
		8. `Having condition` : if there is any variable and only two possible values are only possible suppose there is X
		    and if X is 10 then make it 5 and if 5 then make 10 then `X = 10 ^ 5 ^ X;` this line this do the exact condition. 
		9. `2 important identities` : `((a^b) + (2*(a&b)))` use this to get a+b or `((a|b) + (a&b))` both will give a+b. 
		10. `To find out number of set bits in a number in c++` : 
			1. `if X is int` : `__builtin_popcount(x);` this will give the numbe of set bits in integer x.
			2. `if X is long long` : `__builtin_popcountll(X)` this will tell set bits for long long X.
